<ArticleLayout slug="pinterest-pin-specs" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">A Pinterest pin is 2:3, or 1000 by 1500 pixels, by Pinterest's own recommendation. Two staples of the size guides, the "long pin" and the Idea Pin, are not current Pinterest formats: one was never on a Pinterest page, the other was retired in 2023.</p>

  <h2>Pinterest pin size in 2026: what size should a pin be?</h2>

  <p>Pinterest pin size in 2026 is 1000 by 1500 pixels at a 2:3 ratio, as a PNG or JPEG of up to 20 MB from a computer or 32 MB in the app. Pinterest warns that a pin taller than 2:3 might get cut off in the feed. hubStudio can make the file; you post it to Pinterest yourself.</p>

  <p>Reviewed October 15, 2026. Every number below was read that day on Pinterest's own sites. The dates of the format changes come from Pinterest's announcements. The help pages carry no date, so each row is dated by the read. In the tables, "Help" means Pinterest's Help Center and "Business" its business site. Where two Pinterest pages disagree, both values are printed and each page is named.</p>

