  <blockquote class="evidence">Pinterest's video specs take MP4, MOV or M4V files encoded in H.264 or H.265, up to 2GB, from 4 seconds to 15 minutes long, in any shape between 1:2 and 1.91:1, and recommend square or vertical (2:3, 4:5 or 9:16).</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Pinterest Help Center, "Review ad specs," read October 15, 2026. https://help.pinterest.com/en/business/article/pinterest-product-specs</p>

  <p>Pinterest's video specs give shapes, not pixels. The pixel size is advice: Pinterest's creator site recommends 1080 by 1920 at 9:16 for video and asks you to leave room at the top and bottom, where the player's control bar and settings icon sit.</p>

  <p>How long should a video pin run? Pinterest's own pages give three answers.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Three Pinterest pages give three ideal video lengths: 6 to 15 seconds for a video ad (the Help Center's specs), 15 to 60 seconds (the Help Center's article on pin performance) and 45 to 90 seconds (Pinterest's creator site). Each is Pinterest's advice, with no method published.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Pinterest Help Center and Pinterest Create, read October 15, 2026. https://help.pinterest.com/en/business/article/pin-performance-and-distribution</p>

  <p>Our own rule of thumb, not Pinterest's: cut an ad short and let an organic how-to run longer. Captions are the other thing to plan for. Pinterest generates them automatically and the creator can't edit or style them, its help center says, so words that must read right belong in the picture.</p>

  <h2>How many images can a Pinterest carousel have?</h2>

  <p>Two to five. Collections take more, and that's where the "up to 24" in some size guides comes from.</p>

