  <h2>What should you check before you post a pin?</h2>

  <p>Check the file before you hit Publish. Once a pin is live, its image, video or audio can't be edited, Pinterest's help says; the fix is a new pin.</p>

  <p>The Create Pin form also asks about AI. Its "Mark as AI-Modified" toggles cover content made completely or partly with AI, and content showing an AI-generated person.</p>

  <p>Scheduling depends on which page you read. The help on creating and scheduling pins says a business account can publish up to 30 days ahead, with up to 10 pins scheduled at once. The pin performance article says two weeks.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Full-screen video can be downloaded.</strong> For 9:16 video pins, you choose whether people can download them; a download carries your username as a watermark.</li>
    <li><strong>Up to 10 at a time.</strong> On a computer, one upload takes up to 10 images or 10 videos, and each becomes its own pin. Mixing pictures and video in one pin takes the Pinterest app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How do you make Pinterest files in hubStudio?</h2>

  <p>hubStudio doesn't publish or schedule to Pinterest, and its editors have no Pinterest preset. You make the file in hubStudio, download it, and pin it yourself in Pinterest's Create Pin.</p>

  <p>For a picture, start in the <a href="/app/create">Image studio</a> with a portrait or vertical Shape (the choices depend on the engine). The ChatGPT Image engines also offer Tall (1:3), which is past 2:3 and risks the cut.</p>

  <p>Then open it in the <a href="/app/image-tools">Image editor</a>. In Crop, pick Free and drag the box to two wide by three tall, reading the pixel size the editor shows under the formats. Apply the crop. In Save, choose PNG or JPG (the two files Pinterest's pin specs list) and type 1000 in Width. The height follows, because the proportions stay locked, and lands at 1500 on a true 2:3 crop. Download it, or save a copy in the Assets Library. The Image editor is free and works in your browser.</p>

  <p>For video, the <a href="/app/video-tools">Video editor</a>'s Format panel has a Vertical frame at 9:16 and 1080 by 1920, plus Portrait (4:5) and Square (1:1). All three sit inside the shapes Pinterest recommends. It writes an MP4, at 1080p or 720p.</p>

  <p>When you upload a file you made with an AI engine, the Mark as AI-Modified toggles on Pinterest's Create Pin form are the place to say so.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/resources/insights/instagram-post-sizes-2026">Instagram post sizes guide</a> in the <a href="/resources/specs">platform specs library</a> covers the other feed most pins start from. Teams that want the pins made for them can brief the <a href="/services/design/social-media">social media design service</a>; product pins for a store sit with the <a href="/services/design/ecommerce">ecommerce design service</a>.</p>

