  <h2>FAQ</h2>

  <h3>What size should a Pinterest pin be?</h3>

  <p>Pinterest recommends 1000 by 1500 pixels, a 2:3 ratio, for a standard pin. Upload a PNG or JPEG of up to 20 MB from a computer or 32 MB in the app. Pinterest converts every upload to an 8-bit RGB JPEG, so it suggests PNG in sRGB to avoid losing quality. It publishes no minimum size.</p>

  <h3>What aspect ratio does Pinterest use?</h3>

  <p>2:3 for image pins, by Pinterest's recommendation. Carousels take 1:1 or 2:3. Video can run anywhere from 1.91:1 wide to 1:2 tall, and Pinterest recommends square or vertical: 1:1, 2:3, 4:5 or 9:16. Its creator site recommends 1080 by 1920 at 9:16 for video.</p>

  <h3>What happens if my pin is too tall?</h3>

  <p>Pinterest says it might get cut off in people's feeds, and stops there: no height where the cut starts, no size for a tall pin. The 1000 by 2100 "long pin" that many size guides print isn't on any Pinterest page. Build at 2:3, or split a long graphic into a carousel of two to five images.</p>

  <h3>What are the Pinterest video pin specs?</h3>

  <p>MP4, MOV or M4V, encoded in H.264 or H.265, up to 2GB, from 4 seconds to 15 minutes, in any shape between 1.91:1 and 1:2, with square or vertical recommended. Pinterest's pages disagree on the ideal length: 6 to 15 seconds for an ad, 15 to 60 seconds, or 45 to 90 seconds on its creator site.</p>

  <h3>How many images can a Pinterest carousel have?</h3>

  <p>Two to five, by Pinterest's specs, each a PNG or JPEG of up to 20 MB at 1:1 or 2:3. A carousel built from a product catalog under the sales objective can hold 2 to 10 images and videos. The "up to 24" figure belongs to collections, which take one hero and up to 24 smaller pictures.</p>

  <h3>Can I schedule Pinterest pins from hubStudio?</h3>

  <p>No. hubStudio publishes to LinkedIn, Instagram, Facebook, TikTok (Beta) and X, and doesn't connect to Pinterest. Make and download the file in hubStudio, then use Pinterest's own Create Pin. A business account can publish later from there, up to 30 days ahead by Pinterest's help on scheduling.</p>
